  "findings": [
    "alloca, signal-hook and tree-house-bindings compile pinned C sources into OUT_DIR.",
    "anyhow/proc-macro2/thiserror/heapless/rustix run compiler probes and clean only their OUT_DIR probe children.",
    "serde/serde_core/rustversion/unicode-general-category generate owned OUT_DIR files.",
    "pulldown-cmark generation is gated by gen-tests; normal release does not enable it.",
    "libc extra FreeBSD/emcc discovery is inapplicable to declared Windows/Linux hosts; environment excludes LIBC_CI and unstable overrides."
  ],
  "limitation": "Review of pinned hook entrypoints and relevant native filesystem/process branches, not a complete security audit of dependency code. Availability does not mean every hook/conditional branch executes.",
  "policy": "Reviewed pinned hooks emit target/compiler cfg, probe the selected rustc, generate into Cargo OUT_DIR or compile pinned C sources through installed cc/MSVC. All OUT_DIR, caches and temporary paths are owned. Windows import-library hooks link pinned crate libraries. First-party grammar download/build disabled. No rustc bootstrap/wrapper/CI overrides or gen-tests feature; no dependency installation outside ownership.",
